  <equipmenttech equipmenttechid="mounts" type="3" name="Mount Training" wikides="“It's hard to lead a cavalry charge if you think you look funny on a horse.” -- Adlai E. Stevenson  &#x00A;&#x00A;By the middle ages, animal husbandry had become an art form. Horses were bread for speed, stamina and endurance; trained respond to rider's battle commands and even bit and kicked enemies. For many a knight, his mount was itself a potent weapon.">
