  <equipmenttech equipmenttechid="wrist" type="11" name="Gauntlets" wikides="“A sword never kills anybody; it is a tool in the killer's hand.” --  Lucius Annaeus Seneca &#x00A;&#x00A;Hand protection was key in medieval combat. Crossguards on swords were a start, but soldiers soon found it prudent to wear gauntlets as well, to keep their fingers safe from errant blows. As the technology improved, gauntlets were able to offer better protection without interfering with grip.">
