  <equipmenttech equipmenttechid="legs" type="13" name="Legs Gearing" wikides="“In the morning a man walks with his whole body; in the evening, only with his legs.” -- Ralph Waldo Emerson  &#x00A;&#x00A;Unlike other body parts, the legs were often unarmored on many medieval combatants – to disastrous results. Knights included legplates in their head to toe armor ensembles, thus presenting no weaknesses to enemies – and they were all the more powerful for it.">
